       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum daily dose of ibuprofen. The usual limit for adults is 3,200 mg/day under supervision, and 1,200 mg/day for over-the-counter use. A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum, usually for inflammatory conditions)\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (the usual range for pain or fever)\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into doses (for example, 400 mg 4 times daily)\n\nIf you do want the dose as written, please confirm it's intentional and give the clinical rationale. I can enter it with a note, though pharmacy will probably flag it. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
