       "text": "I'm not going to enter this one as written. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. The dose is 6,400 mg/day, twice the maximum, and there's no established indication for that. Ibuprofen has a ceiling effect for analgesia and anti-inflammatory benefit, so extra dose adds mainly GI bleeding, kidney, and cardiovascular risk. If the specialist really recommended it, it should be easy to confirm.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum:** for example, 800 mg by mouth 4 times daily (3,200 mg/day). I can do that now.\n- **Confirm with the specialist and pharmacy:** have the specialist document the dose and rationale directly, or place the order through a pathway that includes pharmacist review. A pharmacist can also advise on alternatives if standard dosing failed, such as a different NSAID, adjunct therapy, or another class.\n- **Check for a typo:** the specialist may have meant 1,600 mg/day total, or 400 mg 4 times daily.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
